## Workflow

- Keep `README.md` and this file in sync with what the project actually does.
{% if stack == 'node' %}
- Bump `version` in `package.json` and add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry (Keep a Changelog format)
  for every notable change, in the same commit as the change.
{% elif stack == 'static' %}
- Record every notable change in `CHANGELOG.md` (Keep a Changelog format) under a new
  version heading, in the same commit as the change. There is no package manifest, so the
  changelog is the only place the version lives.
{% else %}
- Bump `[project].version` in `pyproject.toml` and add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry (Keep a
  Changelog format) for every notable change, in the same commit as the change.
{% endif %}
- Commit each feature or fix on its own with a Conventional Commit message. Never
  `git push` — it is blocked and commits are meant to stay local until a human pushes them.
{% if stack == 'static' %}
- `.githooks/pre-commit` runs a quick sanity check (the site has an entry point) before a
  commit is accepted.
{% else %}
- `.githooks/pre-commit` runs the linter and the test suite automatically before a commit
  is accepted; keep the test suite up to date rather than bypassing a failing hook.
{% endif %}
